# ForteZar CyberEye — Dual-Use Security Disclosure

ForteZar CyberEye is a defensive web-security utility intended for developers, CI pipelines, security teams, and authorized security assessments.

The package performs passive, externally observable checks such as HTTPS enforcement, security headers, CORS configuration, cookie attributes, mixed content, insecure form actions, and related web-security posture signals. It also includes network-safety controls designed to reduce misuse and server-side request forgery risk, including private/non-public target blocking by default, redirect validation, DNS answer validation, and socket pinning.

CyberEye does not include brute-force attacks, credential attacks, destructive requests, exploit delivery, stealth/evasion features, or automated exploitation. Users must only scan systems they own or are explicitly authorized to assess.

Because security assessment capabilities can be dual-use, this package is declared as dual-use under npm's security-content policy. Its intended purpose is defensive security, secure software development, CI/CD security checks, education, and authorized testing.

Project security policy and responsible-use guidance are available in SECURITY.md and README.md in the source repository.
